<!--
    kuna issue testcase: no AIF gap entry starts on a literal-pool word
    (`option aifpoolslide on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants mid-function entries; the largest
                class left sits one literal-pool word before a real function,
                whose start it hides.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the AIF gap-walk accept
                (`analyzers/aif/kuna_aifpoolslide.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option aifpoolslide on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `poolslide_le32` (generator `poolslide_le32.py` beside it): a
    stripped Thumb ELF whose `_start` calls 22 leaves that open with
    `movs r3,#n; adds r0,r0,r3`, `user` at 0x81f8, which loads the pool word
    at 0x81fc (0x20000124, an SRAM address) with `ldr r0,[pc,#0]`, and `taker`
    at 0x8208, which jumps to `h3` at 0x8210 through `adr r1,h3`.  The
    unreferenced `lone` at 0x8200 follows the pool.  The pool word's high half
    reads as `movs r0,#0`, and with `lone`'s first `adds` it matches the
    leaves' prologue.  Both passes use `mode reliable` with the Listing and the
    gap walk on, as `kuna functions` runs on a large ARM image.

    Pass 1 (`option aifpoolslide off`) reproduces the bug: the gap walk lists
    sub_81fe, on the pool word, and claims `lone` as its body.
    Pass 2 (shipped default) plants that accept on `lone` itself: sub_8200.
    `adr` loads nothing, so `h3`'s first word is not a pool word and `h3` stays
    at its own address in both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/poolslide_le32</com>
  <com>mode reliable</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option aif on</com>
  <com>option aifpoolslide off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/poolslide_le32</com>
  <com>mode reliable</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option aif on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>phase catalog aifpoolslide</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
